# 描述: 必考词Unit02核心词汇

{{bachelor}}{{/ˈbætʃələr}}{{n. 学士；单身汉}}{{He earned a bachelor's degree in computer science.}}
{{bail}}{{/beɪl}}{{n./v. 保释；保释金；舀水}}{{The suspect was released on bail.}}
{{ban}}{{/bæn}}{{v./n. 禁止；禁令}}{{The government imposed a ban on smoking in public places.}}
{{bankrupt}}{{/ˈbæŋkrʌpt}}{{adj./v. 破产的；使破产}}{{The company went bankrupt due to poor management.}}
{{barely}}{{/ˈbeəli}}{{adv. 仅仅；几乎不}}{{He barely passed the exam.}}
{{barrier}}{{/ˈbæriər}}{{n. 障碍；屏障}}{{Language can be a barrier to communication.}}
{{batch}}{{/bætʃ}}{{n. 一批；一组}}{{The first batch of products was sold out quickly.}}
{{beam}}{{/biːm}}{{n./v. 光束；横梁；微笑}}{{She beamed with joy when she heard the news.}}
{{behalf}}{{/bɪˈhɑːf}}{{n. 代表；利益}}{{I am writing on behalf of the entire team.}}
{{behavio(u)r}}{{/bɪˈheɪvjər}}{{n. 行为；举止}}{{The child's behavior has improved significantly.}}
{{beneficial}}{{/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl}}{{adj. 有益的；有利的}}{{Regular exercise is beneficial to health.}}
{{benefit}}{{/ˈbenɪfɪt}}{{n./v. 好处；受益}}{{Regular exercise has many health benefits.}}
{{betray}}{{/bɪˈtreɪ}}{{v. 背叛；泄露}}{{He felt betrayed by his closest friend.}}
{{bias}}{{/ˈbaɪəs}}{{n./v. 偏见；偏向}}{{The report was criticized for its political bias.}}
{{bind}}{{/baɪnd}}{{v. 捆绑；约束}}{{The contract binds both parties to the agreement.}}
{{blaze}}{{/bleɪz}}{{n./v. 火焰；燃烧；闪耀}}{{The fire blazed throughout the night.}}
{{blend}}{{/blend}}{{v./n. 混合；融合}}{{The coffee blend has a unique flavor.}}
{{block}}{{/blɒk}}{{n./v. 街区；阻塞}}{{The fallen tree blocked the road.}}
{{bloom}}{{/bluːm}}{{v./n. 开花；繁盛}}{{The flowers bloom beautifully in spring.}}
{{blunder}}{{/ˈblʌndər}}{{n./v. 大错；犯大错}}{{The company made a blunder by ignoring customer feedback.}}
{{blunt}}{{/blʌnt}}{{adj./v. 钝的；直率的；使变钝}}{{He is known for his blunt manner of speaking.}}
{{boast}}{{/bəʊst}}{{v./n. 自夸；夸耀}}{{He boasted about his achievements to everyone.}}
{{bold}}{{/bəʊld}}{{adj. 大胆的；醒目的}}{{She made a bold decision to start her own business.}}
{{bond}}{{/bɒnd}}{{n./v. 纽带；联系；结合}}{{The mother and child share a strong emotional bond.}}
{{boom}}{{/buːm}}{{n./v. 繁荣；隆隆声}}{{The tech industry experienced a boom in the 2000s.}}
{{boost}}{{/buːst}}{{v./n. 促进；增加}}{{The new policy will boost the economy.}}
{{brace}}{{/breɪs}}{{v./n. 支撑；做好准备；使振作}}{{They braced themselves for the incoming storm.}}
{{brake}}{{/breɪk}}{{n./v. 刹车；制动器}}{{He hit the brakes to avoid the collision.}}
{{breach}}{{/briːtʃ}}{{n./v. 违反；缺口；突破}}{{The company was in breach of contract.}}
{{breakthrough}}{{/ˈbreɪkθruː}}{{n. 突破；重大进展}}{{Scientists have made a breakthrough in cancer research.}}
{{breed}}{{/briːd}}{{v./n. 繁殖；品种}}{{This farm breeds high-quality cattle.}}
{{brief}}{{/briːf}}{{adj./n. 简短的；摘要}}{{He gave a brief summary of the report.}}
{{brilliant}}{{/ˈbrɪliənt}}{{adj. 杰出的；明亮的}}{{She is a brilliant scientist with many achievements.}}
{{brisk}}{{/brɪsk}}{{adj. 活跃的；兴隆的；凉爽的}}{{Business has been brisk this quarter.}}
{{broad}}{{/brɔːd}}{{adj. 宽阔的；广泛的}}{{The road is broad enough for four lanes.}}
{{browse}}{{/braʊz}}{{v. 浏览；吃草}}{{She browsed through the magazine while waiting.}}
{{bruise}}{{/bruːz}}{{n./v. 淤伤；擦伤}}{{He fell and bruised his knee.}}
{{budget}}{{/ˈbʌdʒɪt}}{{n./v. 预算；编预算}}{{The government increased the education budget this year.}}
{{bulk}}{{/bʌlk}}{{n. 大批；大部分；体积}}{{The bulk of the work has been completed.}}
{{bulletin}}{{/ˈbʊlətɪn}}{{n. 公告；简报}}{{The company issued a bulletin about the new policy.}}
