{{contingent}}{{/kənˈtɪndʒənt}}{{adj./n. 取决于…的；代表团}}{{Our plans are contingent on the weather.}}
{{contract}}{{/ˈkɒntrækt}}{{n./v. 合同；收缩}}{{They signed a contract with the construction company.}}
{{contradict}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt}}{{v. 反驳；与…矛盾}}{{The evidence contradicts his earlier statement.}}
{{contrary}}{{/ˈkɒntrəri}}{{adj./n. 相反的；对立面}}{{On the contrary, I think we should continue.}}
{{contrast}}{{/ˈkɒntrɑːst}}{{n./v. 对比；对照}}{{There is a sharp contrast between the rich and the poor.}}
{{contribute}}{{/kənˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v. 贡献；捐献}}{{Everyone should contribute to the protection of the environment.}}
{{controversial}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl}}{{adj. 有争议的}}{{The new law is highly controversial among citizens.}}
{{convenient}}{{/kənˈviːniənt}}{{adj. 方便的；便利的}}{{The location of the hotel is very convenient for tourists.}}
{{convention}}{{/kənˈvenʃn}}{{n. 大会；惯例；公约}}{{The annual convention will be held in Shanghai.}}
{{convert}}{{/kənˈvɜːt}}{{v. 转变；兑换；改变信仰}}{{The factory was converted into apartments.}}
{{convey}}{{/kənˈveɪ}}{{v. 传达；运输；转让}}{{The painting conveys a sense of peace.}}
{{convince}}{{/kənˈvɪns}}{{v. 使确信；说服}}{{She convinced him to change his mind.}}
{{cooperate}}{{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 合作；配合}}{{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.}}
{{coordinate}}{{/kəʊˈɔːdɪneɪt}}{{v./n. 协调；配合；坐标}}{{She coordinated the efforts of the entire team.}}
{{cope}}{{/kəʊp}}{{v. 应对；处理}}{{She learned to cope with stress through meditation.}}
{{core}}{{/kɔːr}}{{n./adj. 核心；核心的}}{{Innovation is the core of the company's strategy.}}
{{corporate}}{{/ˈkɔːpərət}}{{adj. 公司的；法人的}}{{The company announced a new corporate strategy.}}
{{correspond}}{{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 通信；相当于；符合}}{{The data does not correspond with the previous results.}}
{{corrupt}}{{/kəˈrʌpt}}{{adj./v. 腐败的；使腐败；使堕落}}{{The corrupt official was arrested for bribery.}}
{{counsel}}{{/ˈkaʊnsl}}{{n./v. 忠告；商议；律师}}{{She sought counsel from her advisor.}}
{{counterpart}}{{/ˈkaʊntəpɑːt}}{{n. 对应的人或物；副本}}{{The CEO met with his Chinese counterpart.}}
{{couple}}{{/ˈkʌpl}}{{n. 一对；夫妇；几个}}{{The couple celebrated their 50th wedding anniversary.}}
{{coverage}}{{/ˈkʌvərɪdʒ}}{{n. 覆盖范围；报道；保险范围}}{{The insurance provides coverage for medical expenses.}}
{{crack}}{{/kræk}}{{n./v. 裂缝；破裂}}{{There was a crack in the wall of the old house.}}
{{craft}}{{/krɑːft}}{{n./v. 工艺；手艺；精心制作}}{{She learned the craft of pottery from her grandmother.}}
{{crash}}{{/kræʃ}}{{v./n. 碰撞；坠毁；崩溃}}{{The plane crashed into the mountain due to engine failure.}}
{{credential}}{{/krɪˈdenʃl}}{{n. 证书；资格；凭证}}{{The doctor has impressive credentials.}}
{{crew}}{{/kruː}}{{n. 全体船员；一组工作人员}}{{The film crew worked tirelessly to finish the movie.}}
{{crime}}{{/kraɪm}}{{n. 犯罪；罪行}}{{Crime rates have decreased in recent years.}}
{{crisis}}{{/ˈkraɪsɪs}}{{n. 危机；紧要关头}}{{The financial crisis affected economies worldwide.}}
{{criteria}}{{/kraɪˈtɪəriə}}{{n. 标准；条件}}{{The selection criteria are very strict.}}
{{critical}}{{/ˈkrɪtɪkl}}{{adj. 批评的；关键的；危急的}}{{Critical thinking is an important skill for students.}}
{{criticism}}{{/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm}}{{n. 批评；评论}}{{The policy faced criticism from various groups.}}
{{crucial}}{{/ˈkruːʃl}}{{adj. 至关重要的；决定性的}}{{Education is crucial for the development of a country.}}
{{cultivate}}{{/ˈkʌltɪveɪt}}{{v. 培养；耕种}}{{Schools should cultivate students' creativity.}}
{{curb}}{{/kɜːb}}{{v./n. 抑制；控制；路缘}}{{The government introduced measures to curb inflation.}}
{{curiosity}}{{/ˌkjʊəriˈɒsəti}}{{n. 好奇心；珍品}}{{Children have a natural curiosity about the world.}}
{{currency}}{{/ˈkʌrənsi}}{{n. 货币；通用；流行}}{{The Chinese currency is the renminbi (RMB).}}
{{curriculum}}{{/kəˈrɪkjələm}}{{n. 课程；课程表}}{{The school updated its curriculum to include coding classes.}}
{{curve}}{{/kɜːv}}{{n./v. 曲线；弯曲}}{{The road curves sharply to the left.}}
{{customary}}{{/ˈkʌstəməri}}{{adj. 习惯的；通常的}}{{It is customary to shake hands when meeting someone new.}}
{{cyber}}{{/ˈsaɪbər}}{{adj. 网络的；计算机的}}{{Cyber security is a growing concern for businesses.}}
{{cycle}}{{/ˈsaɪkl}}{{n./v. 循环；骑自行车}}{{The water cycle is essential for life on Earth.}}
